     1	//! Parses a small, line-oriented configuration format into ordered [`Entry`] values.
     2	//!
     3	//! Each data line contains `key = value`. Keys contain only ASCII letters,
     4	//! digits, `_`, and `-`, and are case-sensitive. Spaces and tabs around keys
     5	//! and values are ignored. Empty or space/tab-only lines and lines whose first
     6	//! non-space/tab character is `#` are ignored. Within values, `#` and `=` are
     7	//! literal characters.
     8	//!
     9	//! Values starting with `"` are quoted and support only `\\`, `\"`, `\n`, and
    10	//! `\t` escapes. Other characters, including Unicode, are preserved. Only spaces
    11	//! and tabs may follow a closing quote. Lines end with LF or CRLF; a final line
    12	//! need not have an ending. A carriage return outside CRLF is ordinary text.
    13	//!
    14	//! [`parse`] rejects malformed lines and duplicate keys with a [`ParseError`].
    15	//!
    16	//! # Examples
    17	//!
    18	//! ```
    19	//! let entries = small_config::parse("# preferences\nname = café\nmessage = \"hi\\nthere\"\n")?;
    20	//! assert_eq!(entries[0].key, "name");
    21	//! assert_eq!(entries[0].value, "café");
    22	//! assert_eq!(entries[1].value, "hi\nthere");
    23	//! # Ok::<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>>(())
    24	//! ```
    25	
    26	#![deny(missing_docs)]
